	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg8229"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=9" title="View the profile of Karadana">Karadana</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Female.gif" alt="Female" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 96<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/borg.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I&#039;m a Buff Bish!!!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=9"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:Karadana@mail2hell.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=850.msg8229#msg8229"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=850.msg8229#msg8229">Re: Conviction...no loyalty to their guildees</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2 on:</b> June 04, 2004, 03:59:48 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Well not trying to be mean but..someone that has been there done that would be the right thing to do.. he/she would know what is going to happen and will be quick on what to do.(Beings its your first time in there) And really its not like you would never had the chance to be in time. Its not like its the first and last time you will be there.. I mean I have offered to sit out so someone else can play.. shrug thats just me tho. (and I have 735 aa&#039;s ;p)  A little rash on your guildremoving I would think. But we all have to do what we think is best for us =)<br /><br />Its a learning prossess granted.. but why not have that edge with someone that does know whats in store for you in the Phases. Sometimes you have to do whats best for the raid at that time. And its nothing personal when it happens. Sometimes you have to sit back and look at the big picture.. and not in the cubical you are in =)<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									&#171; <i>Last Edit: June 04, 2004, 04:10:12 am by Karadana</i> &#187;
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=179142" target="_blank"><img src="http://webpost.net/ss/Ssnakess/Karadana-1.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a><br /><div align="center">Exit Summoned under the mobs feet,<br />Atleast I didnt have to stand in line I got front row seats!!!</div>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
