								<a href="mailto:murgen21@yahoo.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=850.msg8247#msg8247"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=850.msg8247#msg8247">Re: Conviction...no loyalty to their guildees</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #8 on:</b> June 04, 2004, 03:05:42 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							It does seem like more importance was placed on trying to win on a first crack at Time than on keeping the members happy.&nbsp; I can see why that would be frustrating.&nbsp; Hope things work out for you, Artic.<br /><br />The design of the first part of Time seems incredibly stupid to me anyway in that it locks some people out.&nbsp; 
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
