								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=850.msg8250#msg8250">Re: Conviction...no loyalty to their guildees</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #11 on:</b> June 04, 2004, 03:31:30 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">And sometimes winning at this game is more important than building confidence and winning the hearts and minds of good people in your guild.</div><br />How about, not wasting the time of 72 other folks by risking a rookie when a veteran is available? I can understand Dissonant&#039;s perspective for pulling... as a app that&#039;s sat outside in TimeA while veterans cleared TimeB I disliked it, but sure didn&#039;t toss a hissy fit.<br /><br />End point, you&#039;ve a valid complaint, but IMO, you overreacted.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
