								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=850.msg8251#msg8251">Re: Conviction...no loyalty to their guildees</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #12 on:</b> June 04, 2004, 03:41:31 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I agree the way he reacted was poor.. Should never make hasty decisions, if you are really upset should just log think it through and discuss it in a calm manner with an officer.&nbsp; Perhaps using those with experience wasn&#039;t the best move, maybe it was -- /shrug I am sure whatever Disso and the officers decided they thought was for the better of the guild.. Can&#039;t ask for anything more than that
						</td>
